# AGENTS.md

Guidance for AI coding agents working inside **{{.ProjectName}}**, a full-stack
Go + Vite/React app scaffolded with [juango](https://github.com/juanfont/juango).

Module path: `{{.ModulePath}}`

## What this project is

A web app with batteries included from juango: OIDC authentication, cookie
sessions (SQLite-backed), admin mode with audit logging, user impersonation, an
admin API/UI, a health endpoint, and optional Redis-backed background tasks.
Your job is to build features on top of this foundation.

## Prerequisites

- **Go** and **Node.js 18+ / npm**.
- The `juango` CLI on your PATH (used by `just dev`). Install with
  `go install github.com/juanfont/juango@latest`.

## Run it

```bash
# 1. Create your config from the example
cp config.example.yml config.yml

# 2. Edit config.yml:
#    - oidc.issuer / oidc.client_id / oidc.client_secret
#    - session.authentication_key and session.encryption_key
#      (each must be EXACTLY 32 bytes; generate with `openssl rand -hex 16`)

# 3. Start dev (Vite + Go server, with proxy)
just dev          # wraps `juango dev`
```

Visit the app at `http://localhost:{{.Port}}`.

Other project commands (`just <name>`):

- `build` — build the frontend then the `{{.ProjectName}}` binary.
- `serve` — run the API server (`go run ./cmd/{{.ProjectName}} serve`).
- `worker` — run the background task worker (requires Redis + `tasks.enabled: true`).
- `test` — run Go tests.
- `db-backup <path>` — back up the SQLite database.
- `db-stats` — show database statistics.

Admin CLI helpers: `make-admin <email>`, `list-admins`, `remove-admin <email>`
(run via the built binary or `go run ./cmd/{{.ProjectName}} <cmd> -c config.yml`).

## Layout

```
{{.ProjectName}}/
├── cmd/{{.ProjectName}}/   # Entry point + CLI commands (serve, worker, admin, db)
├── internal/
│   ├── api/                # HTTP app: route registration + your handlers (app.go)
│   ├── database/           # DB wrapper + sql/schema.sql (squibble-managed)
│   ├── tasks/              # Background task definitions + handler registry
│   └── types/              # Config struct + loading
├── frontend/               # Vite/React SPA (pages, components, contexts, lib)
├── app.go                  # Wires config -> DB -> API -> server
├── config.example.yml
└── justfile
```

## Where to add things

- **API routes** — `internal/api/app.go`, at the comment
  `Add your application-specific routes here` inside `registerRoutes()`. Wrap
  handlers with `a.sessionMiddleware.RequireAuth(...)` (optionally
  `RequireAdmin` / `RequireAdminMode`) like the existing routes.
- **Background tasks** — define a task type + handler (copy
  `internal/tasks/dummy.go`), then register it in `internal/tasks/registry.go`
  at the comment `Add your application-specific task handlers here`. Enqueue from
  API handlers via `a.taskClient` (see `internal/api/tasks.go`). Requires
  `tasks.enabled: true`, a reachable `redis.addr`, and a running `just worker`.
- **Database tables** — edit `internal/database/sql/schema.sql` below the comment
  `Add your application-specific tables below`. Keep statements idempotent
  (`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`). The schema is managed by squibble — see
  `internal/database/README.md` for the greenfield vs. migration-rule workflow.
- **Frontend routes** — `frontend/src/App.tsx`, at the comment marker inside the
  `Layout` route (next to the existing `admin/*` routes). Add a `Route` and a
  matching page under `frontend/src/pages/`.

